      <h2>It's the enzyme natto produces while it ferments, and it's been in the Japanese diet for generations.</h2>
      <p>Natto is fermented soybeans, a traditional breakfast food in Japan. During fermentation the Bacillus subtilis culture produces nattokinase, an enzyme studied for its role in supporting healthy fibrin balance and circulation. Large studies of Japanese adults have linked higher natto intake with better long-term outcomes, which is why longevity keeps coming up in the clips. Lucent puts 10,800 FU of it in one enteric-coated capsule, then adds serrapeptase, lumbrokinase and vitamin K2.*</p>
